@up UP link: India's newest **coin mint** is at **Noida** (UP, 1988), one of four. The RBI has regional offices in **Lucknow and Kanpur**, and **SIDBI** is headquartered in **Lucknow**.

@trap
**M3 = M1 + time deposits; money multiplier = M3/M0.** **Decimal coins 1957.** **Minimum reserve Rs. 200 crore (gold Rs. 115 crore).** Coins and Re. 1 note = **Government**; the RBI issues the other notes. **Mints: Mumbai, Kolkata, Hyderabad, Noida.** Fall in inflation = prices rising **more slowly**. **Debtors gain.** **Core = headline − food − fuel.** **WPI: Commerce Ministry; CPI-IW: Labour Bureau; DA uses CPI-IW.** **RBI 1935, nationalised 1949.** Repo: RBI lends; reverse repo: RBI borrows. **CRR up = less liquidity.** **Credit creation = commercial banks.**
@end

@heatmap

@pattern
RBI tools (CRR, SLR, repo) and inflation basics are asked in almost every paper. Recent papers (2017-2021) added **core inflation**, **Operation Twist**, CPI facts and the WPI publisher. Questions on exact policy rates on a given date also appear.
@end

@next
Likely next angles: the **2025 rate cuts** (repo 6.50% → 5.25%), the **CRR cut to 3%**, the **new CPI and GDP base years**, the **inflation-target review** (2026), the **digital rupee (e₹)**, and **UPI** growth.
@end
